# Harness versions the matrix pins: the single place a version changes.
#
# *_PINNED is the fleet-relevant release each PINNED lane runs: a red there
# is OUR bug and blocks a release. The LATEST lane overrides it with
# CODEX_VERSION=latest (etc.) at invocation; a red there is vendor drift and
# is reported, never treated as a straza regression (.github/workflows/
# harness.yml).
#
# Floors (asserted by check -gate floor per lane):
#   codex 0.124.0   hooks GA + requirements.toml managed hook support
#                   (the pinned floor); below it every gate is vacuous: codex
#                   ignores the file.
# Windows-only context (NOT asserted here, because no lane runs on Windows):
#   codex 0.145.0   hook-command quoting fix. 0.146.0 broke the QUOTED exe
#                   form on Windows again, which the single-token shim
#                   (installcodexshim.go) works around. The Linux
#                   spawn path tolerates quotes on 0.144 and 0.146, verified
#                   both ways, so this matrix pins tolerance (cases/quoted-
#                   command.toml.tmpl) and cannot reproduce the Windows kill.
# Every value below ran its full lane green before it was pinned: codex
# with g3-live and g4-e2e, gemini with live BeforeTool and the trust
# battery, claude with all four key-free gates. The codex --oss/ollama
# empty-name defect still holds at 0.147.0, so the live-tool observation
# stands.
CODEX_PINNED=0.147.0
GEMINI_PINNED=0.55.1
CLAUDE_PINNED=2.1.233

# Live-model plumbing (codex g3-live/g4-e2e): native ollama tarball unpacked
# into .tools/, docker-free. The agent-e2e lane's ollama/ollama:0.6.8 image is
# too old here, because codex 0.146 --oss requires ollama >= 0.13.4. With
# codex 0.146.0 and ollama 0.32.5, codex --oss drives ollama over
# /v1/responses and small non-gpt-oss models arrive with an EMPTY tool-call
# name ("unsupported call:"), so unified-exec dispatch is unreliable. The
# live gates hard-assert turn-end events and retry the tool event on an
# attempt ladder.
OLLAMA_PINNED=0.32.5
CODEX_OSS_MODEL=qwen3:1.7b

# python-kit lane (lanes/python-kit.sh): the framework releases the PINNED
# channel proves kits/python against. The LATEST channel overrides with
# PYTHON_KIT_VERSION=latest and takes whatever pip resolves today. Only these
# five dists are pinned. Transitive deps float, because they are not what the
# lane certifies. This exact set resolved from a fresh `pip install
# ./kits/python[all extras]` and ran the full suite 109/109, zero skips,
# STRAZA_KIT_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1.
LANGCHAIN_PINNED=1.3.15
LANGGRAPH_PINNED=1.2.11
OPENAI_AGENTS_PINNED=0.21.0
CLAUDE_AGENT_SDK_PINNED=0.2.139
DEEPAGENTS_PINNED=0.7.6
